# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/ IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED.
#
# This repository tracks example harness settings on purpose, because "merging a hook does not
# install one" is the single most expensive lesson in this whole toolkit: a settings file nobody can
# read is indistinguishable from one that is wired correctly. Today that is
# .claude/settings.example.json, which shows the hand-wiring for the blanket-stage guard -- one of
# the controls no installer covers (see docs/HOOKS.md and INSTALL.md).
#
# THE RULE, not a census: anything tracked under .claude/ MUST carry `.example.` in its name. The
# harness loads settings.json and settings.local.json only, so an `.example.` file is inert by
# construction and cannot become a control that looks installed. The machine-local files are ignored
# below.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Machine-local overrides. The convention throughout: anything with `.local.` in its name belongs to
# one checkout on one machine and must never be committed.
*.local.*
.claude/settings.local.json

# Coordination state lives in the git directory (<git-common-dir>/ccx-coord), so it is uncommittable
# by construction and needs no rule here. These are the strays that escape it.
*.log
ccx-doctor-report.*

# Language runtimes a project setup hook may create inside a worktree.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Build output of the documentation site. site-build.yml writes _site at the repository root and
# scripts/site/build_redirect.py writes _redirect; both are generated on every run and neither is
# ever the source of anything. Gemfile.lock is deliberately NOT listed: site-build.yml explains that
# a lock file is wanted eventually and is waiting on a green run to produce a trustworthy one, so
# ignoring it here would quietly cancel that.
_site/
_redirect/
.jekyll-cache/
.jekyll-metadata

# Local state written by the wrangler CLI when someone runs it by hand against the Pages project.
# CI authenticates from repository secrets and never writes this.
.wrangler/

# Editors and desktops.
.vs/
.vscode/*.local.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
